## Goal

Use only the frozen `self_activation.pcap` to reconstruct the full structural ViP timeline around packets 200..240 after the entrance device-video boundary.

This is the follow-up to P50. It is intended to bind, without guessing, the sequence around:

- packet 200 device `0x0008`;
- device `0x0002` and the official-client ACK;
- client `0x000a`;
- the next device frame and ACK pair;
- client `0x001a`;
- any request/channel identity first observed after the device-video anchor.

## What it reports

For every reconstructed ViP frame intersecting packets 200..240:

- direction;
- packet range;
- time delta from packet-200 anchor;
- channel class (`CTPP`, `CONTROL`, `OTHER_EXISTING`, `OTHER_NEW`);
- body length;
- structural prefix/action/flags;
- whether it is an ACK-shaped `0x1800` frame;
- same-CTPP, same-direction sequence delta only (never literal sequence values).

For each structural client ACK it also reports the nearest preceding same-CTPP device frame, timing gap, intervening frame count, and the capture-derived reversed tail-address relation, checked only in memory.

## Safety / privacy

Frozen-PCAP analysis only. No network launcher is added.

The report emits no request ids, endpoint/IP/port, protocol addresses, literal sequence values, raw payload, hex/base64 payload, or media bytes. No Comelit traffic, listener changes, HA changes, Door action, self-activation, media signaling, or ACK signaling are performed.

## Tests

Synthetic tests cover bidirectional ordering, exact ACK-to-nearest-device binding, reversed address-role relation, visibility of client `0x000a` / `0x001a`, new-channel classification, sequence-delta-only reporting, pinned capture/window identity, and offline/privacy invariants.

Merge prepares only a read-only CT120 PCAP analysis. It does not authorize a new live packet.

## Problem

CMW 0.4.1 correctly blocked `verified_final` when `logo_application=always` did not use the exact official logo, but the review flow still allowed an earlier failure mode: a generated visual containing a baked-in AI approximation of the project logo could be shown and human-selected before the integrity failure was discovered at finalization.

The loophole came from permissive review wording such as `when technically possible` and from treating generator outputs too directly as A/B/C candidates.

## Fix

- introduces a strict distinction between internal/base drafts and durable review candidates;
- under `logo_application=always`, a social A/B/C is review-ready only after:
  1. the base is verified clear of generated/unverified project branding;
  2. the exact official logo is deterministically composed;
  3. the branded output is bound to the frozen `contract_revision` and exact logo/output SHA-256 evidence;
- adds `scripts/visual-review-gate.py` as an executable fail-closed validator;
- prevents `selected` / `fully_approved` from being reached from non-review-ready visuals;
- adds a targeted recovery path for previously selected visuals with generated/unverified logos: preserve approved text and conceptual preference, repair only the affected visual, and request targeted re-confirmation when pixels/hash change;
- does not force a full A/B/C restart unless concept changes materially or the user asks for one.

## Regression coverage

Adds tests for:

- missing deterministic logo composition evidence;
- generated/unverified branding in the base;
- wrong official-logo SHA;
- raw/base output incorrectly bound as the review asset;
- incorrect candidate count;
- contract language closing the late-logo-failure loophole.

CI now runs this test explicitly.

